{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1520688-how-do-you-play-a-gadgeteer-inspired","id":1520688,"title":"How do you play a gadgeteer inspired?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-15T11:05:06-07:00","id":1520688,"title":"How do you play a gadgeteer inspired?","content":"I love the archetype of the gadgeteer hero (Macguiver, Iron Man, reed richards, Scotty, etc...)\u2014specifically, one capable of jury-rigging devices and solutions on the fly. The problem is, I struggle with the system when I want to portray that. How do you do it? Could you give me some examples? Imagine you're playing a Nova with Iron Man armor who suddenly wants to modify the cannon of his arm so it can shoot water to help put a fire, or you're a talent who just escaped the bad guys and you're in a warehouse, the only way out is the ceiling, but there are tools around, how would you improvise a grappling gun? etc...thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T13:02:38-07:00","id":1520701,"title":"","content":"Use the Super-Science rules. There's a section of jury-rigging, if I recall correctly, that exists specifically to model McGuyver feats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T13:01:15-07:00","id":1520970,"title":"","content":"The Super-Science rules have a kind of rocky presentation in TC: Core, and some of the later games have offered some backdoor refinement and smoothing over of the rough edges. Even then, there are lots of common house rules people adopt. Dataweaver isn't wrong though, a MacGuyver type character is very doable with the super-science rules.<br /> <br /> I highly recommend <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/372295/The-Storyguides-Guide-to-Telling-Stories-A-Guide\" target=\"_blank\">The Storyguides Guide to Telling Stories</a> on the Storypath Nexus, it's pretty cheap and does a really good job going over a lot of rules and doing a better job with presentation than the Core does, it also offers houserules and goes over why they might be a good idea.<br /> <br /> I'm preparing an Aeon game in roll20 and have basically built a TC compendium in handouts. Here is a summary from my super-science handout that rolls in some of the expanded rules from Adventure and some of the ideas from the supplement I mentioned above.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Super Science Creation</b></span><br /> <b>Type</b>: Complex Action<br /> <b>Milestones</b>: Equal to the Rank of the invention (may add Milestones for large or especially complex projects)<br /> <b>Interval</b>: Sessions equal to Rank <i>(This is a house rule, in the Core rules Rank 5 inventions take one chronicle per Milestone)</i><br /> <b>Total Attempts:</b> Total Milestones x2<br /> <b>Skill</b>: Varies by Milestone and type of invention<br /> <b>Difficulty</b>: Equal to Rank<br /> <b>Complication</b>: Varies, but one roll always has a Complication equal to Rank. If not bought off this introduces a Flaw with points equal to the Rank.<br /> <b>Milestone Success:</b> You complete a Milestone, and may purchase stunts with any threshold successes.<br /> <b>Milestone Failure:</b> You fail to complete the Milestone, and introduce 1pt of Flaws to the invention.<br /> <br /> <b>Action Success:</b> You've completed all Milestones and an invention matching your design specs is ready and functional with at least points in Flaws equal to the Rank (in addition to any introduced by Complications or failures). Inventions need to be bought using the Artifact Edge, with a rating equal to the Rank of the invention.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Jury Rigging</b></b><br /> Uses the same system as above, but the Interval for each Milestone is a single round, and the invention will have a number of flaws equal to twice the Rank (in addition to any introduced by Complications or Failures). if the invention is Inspired or Powered one of the Flaws should be One Time Use or Self-Destructive, an invention decades ahead of its time thrown together in moments is rarely stable.<br /> <br /> <b>Super Science Stunts </b>(Some of these are from Adventure)<br /> You can use threshold successes to purchase special stunts to help with invention process or the improve the final product.<ul><li><b>Flaw Prevention (Varies) -</b> Add 1e per success spent to your next invention roll (even if your next roll uses the same skill)</li> <li><b>On Time, Under Budget (4s) </b>- Remove a Milestone from the total required for the invention.</li> <li><b>Made to Fit (3s)</b> - Increase or decrease the Size Scale of the item by 1 per 3e spent.</li> <li><b>Puissance and Potency (3s) </b>- Increase an aspect of Scale (Power, Durability, etc...) by 1, but reduce the total amount of Enhancement by 1.</li> </ul><b>Invention Rank</b><br /> <b>New Designs vs. Upgrades </b>(This is from Adventure) - When creating a Super Science inventions you can choose to create something from scratch, or upgrade an existing design.<br /> <br /> When upgrading an existing design it starts with all of the Tags it would normally have (minus the Quality Tag or others that offer Enhancement), and treat the interval between Milestones as if the invention were two Ranks less, but you must acquire a version of what you wish to upgrade using the Wealth Edge. Perhaps more importantly you reduce the time between intervals by 2 sessions, down to a minimum of one. (examples, a hyper-precise laser carbine that offers far more Enhancement than a normal one, a shuttle that can go from the depths of the ocean to the moon)<br /> <br /> When creating a new design you're not bound the form or function of any existing invention, and you gain the ability to swap dots of Edges for additional points of Tags on a 1:1 basis. (examples a personal hover chair with orbiting laser drones, an infinitely variable personal firearm powered by nanotech, a slug thrower that uses hard light holograms for ammo, biotech not based on any existing noetic template but engineered from the base-pairs up)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","user":"literatzi","date":". 08-26-2023, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T13:27:14-07:00","id":1520972,"title":"","content":"A common critique of the Super Science rules is that they take too long if you're not jury-rigging, there are some ways around this without houseruling the intervals between Milestones.<br /> <br /> There is a Technology skill trick called <b>Ahead of Your Time</b> that lets you spend 1 Momentum to just remove a single Milestone from a super science creation. <b>The On Time, Under Budget</b> stunt also lets you remove a Milestone. Talents can use the <b>Eureka!</b> gift which lets you reduce Milestones needed to create an invention by several steps.\u200b<br /> <br /> For a MacGyver character who is jury-rigging a lot I'd recommend the <b>It's Not a Bug, It's a Feature</b> skill trick gives your creation enhancement equal to the points of flaws (which jury rigged creations have lots of) so the arc welder you made out of jumper cables, a generator, and two quarters is really good!<br /> <br /> The <b>R&amp;D</b> Science skill trick lets you reduce the Complication one of your creation rolls will have, reducing the chance of your creation having flaws.<br /> <br /> The <b>Quick Fix</b> gift helps you repair things when you don't have the tools or time to do it right. <b>Sawed Off</b> is a gift that lets you make custom versions of your gear that are smaller and less obtrusive without messing with the super science rules. <b>Hidden Advantage</b> lets you hide things on your person really well, and declare you had something hidden even if you didn't, which could be explained as building things quickly. <b>Device Mogul </b>lets you declare once per scene you have a piece of gear on hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}